From 6183f651aa07c217c9b042461e2e764911fdd771 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:30:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06875/11362] [outer-loop] ARC re86 round-5: honest null, first
 rectangle's L8 route solved

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on re86 finds the fix for round-4's repaint
trap: a two-stage flatten/corridor/compress route, not a resize-tolerance
issue. Flatten the color-11 rectangle to 22x4, traverse the seven-row
corridor, recompress to 4x22 at the upper-right fixture, and cross the
TRUE six-cell background opening at x=44..49 (not the visually-similar
four-cell corridor round 4 tried) -- this route preserved color 11 and
placed the rectangle exactly over all four sockets. The second rectangle
was resized to its target geometry but budget ran out before its
analogous crossing.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 7. Only
the second rectangle's crossing remains as unsolved work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
