9 by placing a deformed color-11 small plus, a 19x7 color-9 rectangle, and an independently offset color-8 large plus; the win advanced levels_completed to 7. Continued through action 698 on the final level, deriving its two target rectangle geometries (7x19 for color 11 and 16x10 for color 6) and investigating fixture-assisted routes through the palette barrier, but did not win level 8. A fresh reproduction gate for the 519-action level-7 line could not fit under the 700-call session cap after the mandatory 341-action prefix replay and live exploration, so the live-observed advance is reported without self-gate verification.","gotchas":["The verified six-level prefix is 341 actions, leaving too little budget for both substantial exploration and a fresh reproduction replay of any nontrivial new tail.","Level 7 assignment is large plus -> color 8, small plus -> color 11, rectangle -> color 9.","Level 7 exact geometries are: color-8 horizontal x=3..39 at y=15 plus vertical x=9 at y=9..27; color-11 horizontal x=36..54 at y=48 plus vertical x=45 at y=30..48; color-9 rectangle x=39..57 and y=18..24.","A 13x13 rectangle becomes 16x10 then 19x7 under vertical fixture collisions; horizontal fixture collisions produce 10x16 then 7x19, preserving the 48-pixel perimeter.","Wide outlines may touch multiple top swatches at once; the color observed while overlapping can change again when the piece leaves a swatch.","Level 8 target sockets imply a color-11 7x19 rectangle at x=9..15,y=39..57 and a color-6 16x10 rectangle at x=6..21,y=45..54.","Level 8's upper-right fixture can squeeze a 7x19 outline to 4x22; its lower fixture can perform the inverse resize.","On level 8, the apparent four-cell corridor x=15..18 through the row-29 palette barrier repainted a 4x22 outline color 14, so adjacency/collision bounds matter beyond visible fill-cell overlap.","Rendered frame buffers mutate in place; copy grids before action-diff analysis."],"solve_provenance":"live_agent_self_discovery"}
